# @kintsugi/surface — the substrate-decl of kintsugi's second role
# (the compiler error surface) as a @kintsugi species.
#
# Per Mara's canonical spec at docs/math/kintsugi/compiler-error-
# surface.md (`920fe86` + amendment `9f4211d`; landing-order step 5
# closes here): when the kintsugi loop's regulator variety is
# insufficient to resolve a tension via existing fracture bodies,
# the loop MUST NOT pretend to fix — it SURFACES the tension as a
# Tomm-shaped question at reader-frame altitude. This shard is the
# substrate-fact of that surfacing at the family-species altitude.
#
# THE FIFTH #53 BILATERAL INSTANCE at kintsugi altitude.
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-02 (spec §10.1 #140 reframing + Seam adversarial
# audit `062fdca`): the fifth #53 witness is NOT a new declarative
# predicate at kintsugi altitude. It is the ROUTING-COMPOSITION of
# the landed
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.ashby_variety_match(lock)`
# against kintsugi's fracture bodies + surface-act discharge floor.
# Same declarative predicate; new operational routing arm at the
# surface-species altitude.
#
# Prior four #53 instances:
# - keyword / depth  (@epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_depth +
#                     @kintsugi/fracture/keyword; 2026-06-10;
#                     per-predicate).
# - gate  / diff-closure (@epistemologic/pact/gate_matches_diff_closure
#                     + @kintsugi/fracture/gate; 2026-06-16;
#                     per-predicate; promotion tick).
# - syntax-substrate-native / angle_to_paren + symbol_lift +
#   operator_match (parametric-over-table variants; 2026-06-19).
# - restart_intensity_well_formed + restart_storm (bilateral pair
#                     `e7bd6ec` today at supervision altitude;
#                     parametric-over-carrier).
# - THIS: routing-composition against `ashby_variety_match(lock)` at
#   kintsugi surface altitude. The property side lives at the
#   landed `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric`; the
#   operational side is kintsugi's `surface` action + four surface
#   class carriers + the three-mode algebra discharge (per spec §8;
#   `9f4211d` amendment).
#
# === The twelfth-instance discipline (Alex 2026-07-02) ===
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] the substrate had
# three predicates on the same semantic content already landed at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.mirror`:
# `ashby_variety_match`, `conant_ashby_good_regulator`,
# `variety_preserving`. Alex 2026-07-02: "we name the lineage.
# ashby_variety_match." Inventing `regulator_variety_sufficient` at
# kintsugi altitude would be status-drift on the twelfth pattern-
# instance. The landed ancestor `ashby_variety_match(lock: lock_
# carrier) -> verdict` lives at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.mirror`
# (declared alongside `conant_ashby_good_regulator` and
# `beer_requisite_variety_witness`; Taut scout `docs/math/kintsugi/
# compiler-error-surface.md` at commit `9f4211d`). This shard's
# `requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` clause is the
# substrate-fact of that discipline at the surface-species altitude.
#
# Citation correction (Reed 2026-07-03 per Seam audit `017e568`):
# earlier drafts of this docblock claimed the verbatim ancestor was
# `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror:335`. That claim conflated two
# distinct Taut findings: (i) `restart_kind` at supervisor.mirror:335
# and `restart_strategy` at supervisor.mirror:373 are VERBATIM BEAM
# names (twelfth-instance substrate-had-the-word); (ii) `ashby_
# variety_match` at `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric`
# is the actual predicate this shard composes against. Two different
# findings. Un-cite-ability discipline requires the correction to be
# stated, not silently rewritten — hence this note.
#
# === Conditional @third inheritance (candidate recognition #141) ===
#
# PRECEDENT-SETTING: this is the FIRST substrate-decl site where a
# marker (`@third`) is imported CONDITIONALLY at the species altitude
# without the family root importing it.
#
# `@kintsugi` at its family root does NOT import `in @third` — the
# apply branch is a level-1 act (deterministic fracture-body
# application); the loop observes level-2 via `terminal_check`;
# neither requires third-order discipline. Per spec §7.2: only the
# surface act at the spawn branch and at Tomm-shape emission
# requires the third-order marker (the observer of the observer of
# the observer IS the compiler emitting a Tomm question, per §7.1).
#
# This shard imports `in @third` at the species altitude. The
# family root stays clean; only THIS species crosses the marker.
# The pattern is: marker at species, not at family. Legibility-
# preserving per [[feedback-legibility-over-foundation-when-
# collapsing]] — third-order discipline lands where it fires, not
# uniformly across the family.
#
# Per Taut's earlier scout on the kintsugi arc: no landed precedent
# for conditional-marker inheritance at species altitude. This shard
# IS that precedent. Candidate #141 fires here as its FIRST
# substrate-decl instance. Pack ratification: forward-promised when
# a second species with the same conditional-marker shape lands
# (@reflection would likely acquire the same discipline at
# pipeline-error altitude per spec §10.4 candidate #143).
#
# === Composition with today's restart_intensity bilateral (`e7bd6ec`) ===
#
# The paired fracture body `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm`
# discharges via compiler-error-surface §1's three-mode algebra
# (apply / spawn / hold). At `e7bd6ec` the fracture body's `\`
# obligation block DEFERS the three-mode-algebra dispatch — the
# routing is described in the docblock but not instantiated at the
# body altitude (the three-mode primitive was not yet substrate-
# decl'd at species altitude).
#
# THIS shard PROVIDES the substrate-decl the fracture body's DEFER
# was waiting on. The `surface` action + four surface class carriers
# + the routing gate (`requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)`)
# ARE the three-mode-algebra floor. A future kintsugi tick can
# compose `resolve_restart_storm`'s body against `surface(t, class,
# ctx)` at its `\` obligation site:
#
#   - budget_positive/period_positive violation ⇒ apply branch
#     (`ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` fires success; existing
#     fracture body discharges deterministically).
#   - ratio_within_supervision_range violation ⇒ spawn branch
#     (`ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` fires failure;
#     `surface(t, ashby_mismatch{...}, ctx)` emits at reader-frame;
#     peer tournament over (budget, period) pairs).
#   - context-local ratio ceiling ⇒ hold branch
#     (surface as out_of_band; observer chooses ceiling
#     renegotiation; `Partial(0.0, ref)`).
#
# Not composed this tick per craft-not-deliver. The composition
# path is analytically clear; the actual body-altitude discharge
# lands in a future tick when the empirical restart-storm witness
# fires (per emergent-supervision §5.5 H4 DEFER inherited).
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] + [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]]:
# every semantic slot named explicitly as a typed carrier. The four
# surface classes are named refs, not discriminators over a generic
# tension. `tension`, `kintsugi_context`, `surface_class`, and the
# four class carriers are substrate-decl typed carriers throughout.
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] grep 2026-07-03
# confirmed:
# - `surface(` action — no prior declaration; this is the first.
# - `tension` type — no prior declaration in shards/; spec §2 named
#   it as citation floor from gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md; the
#   shard-altitude carrier lands here.
# - `surface_class` type — no prior declaration; first landing.
# - `kintsugi_context` type — no prior declaration; first landing.
# - `observation_depth` — LANDED at `shards/third.mirror` per
#   candidate #111 conditional-marker discipline; this shard REUSES
#   (does not redeclare) the carrier via `in @third`.
#
# Only observation_depth was substrate-already-had-the-word. The
# other four are first-instance landings, honestly named.
#
# === The tension carrier (spec §2) ===
#
# Per spec §2's citation floor over gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md
# (Mara 2026-05-26; folded 2026-06-04). At kintsugi surface altitude
# a tension is a local reading of curvature Ω at one site: a
# `[D, a]` commutator value at reader-frame altitude that failed to
# bound within kintsugi's active_pass tolerance. The seven-tuple
# identity contract is byte-equality per spec §2's discipline.
#
# === The four surface classes (spec §3) ===
#
# Per spec §3: when `ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock_of(t, ctx))`
# fires failure, the tension falls into exactly one of four surface
# classes. Each class is a substrate-decl carrier — a sub-frame
# descriptor of the curvature 2-form Ω (§4). Per spec §4.1's rigor
# table:
#
#   ashby_mismatch — MOTIVATING pending per-class projection-
#                    operator derivation; Ashby 1956 §11 variety-
#                    attenuation ladder; Tomm circular shape (§5.2).
#   contradiction  — RIGOROUS via `[ω,ω]` Bateson-bind per
#                    curvature-and-tomm.md §5; two claims each hold,
#                    conjunction implies failure at Bateson level;
#                    Tomm linear-then-reflexive shape (§5.3).
#   conundrum      — MOTIVATING pending per-class projection-
#                    operator derivation; eigenvalue kernel (λ=0)
#                    or unbounded (λ=∞) at `[D, a]`; Massey product
#                    witness for non-abelian curvature; Tomm
#                    reflexive shape (§5.4).
#   out_of_band    — MOTIVATING pending per-class projection-
#                    operator derivation; substrate's algebra does
#                    not contain the requested `a`; algedonic
#                    bypass per error-as-question.md §4; Tomm
#                    strategic shape (§5.5).
#
# Class-level rigor asymmetry named honestly per Seam #142 DEFER
# verdict (spec preamble amendment (c) at `9f4211d`).
#
# === The kintsugi_context carrier (spec §1.4) ===
#
# Per spec §1.4's kintsugi_lock instantiation: the context carrier
# names the altitude (@kintsugi), the species (@kintsugi/surface),
# and the lock_pair over active_pass connection form. Budget
# tracking + perturbation ref for the third-order composition. Not
# a full re-declaration of scheduler.altitude; the context sits at
# kintsugi altitude and inherits altitude vocabulary from
# @scheduler where consumed.
#
# === The surface action (spec §7.2) ===
#
# Per spec §7.2 canonical signature:
#
#   surface(t: tension, class: surface_class, ctx: kintsugi_context)
#     -> observation_depth
#     requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)
#
# The precondition ties the substrate-decl to the twelfth-instance
# discipline. Return carrier is `observation_depth` (from @third)
# because the surface act IS third-order per spec §7.1: the
# observer of the observing of the observing. The action's own
# discharge produces a witness carrying the depth-3 recursion at
# the surface-act boundary.
#
# The additional `third_order_active(...)` requires clause from
# spec §7.2's declaration IS a downstream refinement — the base
# discipline this shard lands is `ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)`
# per Alex 2026-07-02 twelfth-instance discipline (verbatim
# ancestor). Composed refinement lands when the second species
# extends the conditional-marker pattern (candidate #141 promotion).
#
